**Summary:** The POC has substantially more engineering capability than a 2.6 score suggests: it has an IncidentSkill, lifecycle rules, semantic validation, DOM→Moondream→Gemini perception, persistence verification, defect-scope separation, reproduction, evidence capture, cleanup and reporting. The problem is that the evidence does not yet demonstrate the thing that matters most for UAT: **repeatedly finding real Incident defects while operating only as a normal UAT persona**. The repository's strongest live-run evidence is a single `INC0000007` lifecycle transition and explicitly documents use of **administrator credentials**, while the benchmark suite itself explicitly describes its FP/FN measurements as simulated. [Incident lifecycle test report](https://github.com/amanpratap1999/UAT_poc/blob/main/docs/incident_lifecycle_test_report.md?utm_source=chatgpt.com) [Phase 5 benchmark audit](https://github.com/amanpratap1999/UAT_poc/blob/main/docs/phase5_acceptance_audit.md?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

**Compared with a competent human:** the POC already has stronger deterministic browser instrumentation and structured post-action verification, but currently trails a human on defect discovery breadth, persona-faithful judgement, negative testing, and demonstrated consistency.

